---
{
  "layout": "layout.njk",
  "permalink": "stories.html",
  "title": "Scripture Story Library · Sanatan Heritage",
  "description": "Browse illustrated stories from verified Vedic, Puranic, epic, Upanishadic and devotional sources.",
  "bodyClass": "stories-page scripture-library-page",
  "ogType": "website",
  "ogImage": "og.png",
  "ogImageAlt": "Sanatan Heritage — Scripture Story Library",
  "noindex": false,
  "search": false,
  "story": false,
  "scripts": ["/assets/js/stories.js"],
  "sourceLink": "sources.html#stories"
}
---
<main data-pagefind-body id="main">
  <section class="collection-hero" id="top">
    <div>
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb"><a href="/index.html">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Scripture Story Library</span></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">THE DIGITAL SCRIPTURE LIBRARY</p>
      <h1>Begin with a text.<br><em>Enter its stories.</em></h1>
      <p>Explore illustrated readers through their verified scriptural homes. Samhitas, Upanishads, Puranas and epics remain clearly distinguished.</p>
      <a class="button" href="#collections">Choose a collection</a>
      <p class="collection-path-link"><a href="/reading-paths.html">Or follow a reading path</a></p>
    </div>
    <figure><img alt="An elder storyteller sharing a manuscript with two listeners beneath a banyan tree" src="/assets/images/story-manuscripts.webp"><figcaption>FROM SACRED TEXTS TO SHARED STORIES</figcaption></figure>
  </section>

  <section class="section scripture-carousel-section" id="collections" aria-labelledby="collections-title">
    <div class="scripture-carousel-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / CHOOSE A SCRIPTURE</p><h2 id="collections-title">Sacred stories,<br><em>held by their texts.</em></h2><p>Across hymns, dialogues, epics and Puranas, sacred stories carry questions of duty, devotion, courage and liberation. Choose a verified collection to meet each account within its own textual home.</p></div>
    <div class="scripture-layer-key" aria-label="Textual layers"><span>Samhita</span><span>Brahmana</span><span>Aranyaka</span><span>Upanishad</span><p>Related layers remain distinct source labels throughout this library.</p></div>
    <div class="scripture-carousel" data-scripture-carousel>
      <button class="scripture-carousel-arrow scripture-carousel-previous" type="button" aria-label="Previous scripture" aria-controls="scripture-carousel-track"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span></button>
      <div class="scripture-carousel-viewport" id="scripture-carousel-viewport" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Scripture collections" tabindex="0">
        <div class="scripture-carousel-track" id="scripture-carousel-track">
          <button class="scripture-carousel-card" type="button" data-collection-link="" data-collection-title="Complete library" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="library">
            <span class="scripture-carousel-category">Library index</span><strong>All verified stories</strong><small>{{ storyCatalog | storyCountForCollection('all') }} readers</small><i aria-hidden="true">Complete collection</i>
          </button>
          {% for category in scriptureCollections.categories %}{% for collection in category.collections %}{% if collection.enabled %}
          <button class="scripture-carousel-card" type="button" data-collection-link="{{ collection.id }}" data-collection-title="{{ collection.title }}" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="library">
            <span class="scripture-carousel-category">{{ category.title }}</span><strong>{{ collection.title }}</strong><small>{{ storyCatalog | storyCountForCollection(collection.id) }} {% if (storyCatalog | storyCountForCollection(collection.id)) == 1 %}story{% else %}stories{% endif %}</small><i aria-hidden="true">{{ collection.eyebrow }}</i>
          </button>
          {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <button class="scripture-carousel-arrow scripture-carousel-next" type="button" aria-label="Next scripture" aria-controls="scripture-carousel-track"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
    </div>
    <p class="scripture-carousel-status" id="scripture-carousel-status" aria-live="polite">Choose a scripture to filter the stories below.</p>
  </section>

  <span id="collection" class="legacy-anchor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <section class="section collection-section scripture-library-results" id="library" aria-labelledby="library-title">
    <div class="collection-contexts">
      <section class="collection-context is-active" data-collection-context="all"><p class="eyebrow">ALL VERIFIED READERS</p><h2 id="library-title">The complete library.</h2><p>Every story appears once here, even when more than one verified collection connects to it. Choose a scripture above to narrow the library.</p></section>
      {% for category in scriptureCollections.categories %}{% for collection in category.collections %}{% if collection.enabled %}
      <section class="collection-context" data-collection-context="{{ collection.id }}" hidden><p class="eyebrow">{{ category.title }} / {{ collection.eyebrow }}</p><h2>{{ collection.title }}</h2><p>{{ collection.description }}</p><p class="collection-distinction"><strong>Source distinction:</strong> {{ collection.note }}</p><a href="#collections">Choose another collection</a></section>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <form class="collection-controls scripture-library-controls" role="search">
      <label class="collection-search">Search this library<input id="story-search" placeholder="Try Nachiketa, courage or Rigveda" type="search"></label>
      <label>Scripture collection<select id="collection-filter"><option value="">All verified stories</option>{% for category in scriptureCollections.categories %}{% for collection in category.collections %}{% if collection.enabled %}<option value="{{ collection.id }}">{{ collection.title }}</option>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}</select></label>
      <button id="clear-filters" type="button">Show all stories</button>
    </form>
    <p aria-live="polite" class="collection-count" id="story-count" role="status">{{ storyCatalog | storyCountForCollection('all') }} full stories</p>
    <div class="collection-grid">
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.savitri.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.savitri.textLayer }}" data-deity="Sages &amp; devotees" data-format="full" data-scripture="Mahabharata" data-theme="Dharma" id="story-savitri-satyavan"><figure><img src="/assets/images/savitri-satyavan-card.webp" alt="Savitri supports Satyavan as Yama approaches through a misty forest, in an imagined scene from the Mahabharata" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SAVITRI &amp; SATYAVAN / STEADFASTNESS</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.savitri.textLayer }}</p><h3>Savitri and Satyavan</h3><p>A princess follows Yama and speaks with wisdom to secure five boons and her husband's return.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.savitri.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.savitri.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#savitri-satyavan">Mahabharata, Vana Parva 293–299</a></p></div></article>

<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.halahala.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.halahala.textLayer }}" data-deity="Shiva" data-format="full" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Compassion" id="story-shiva-poison"><figure><img alt="Shiva with Bhavani beside him, receiving the poison from the cosmic ocean" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/halahala-card.webp"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="featured-label">Featured story</p><p class="eyebrow">SHIVA / COMPASSION</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.halahala.textLayer }}</p><h3>Shiva drinks Halahala</h3><p>When the ocean yields a terrible poison, Shiva acts to protect the worlds.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.halahala.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.halahala.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-shiva-poison">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 8, Chapter 7</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.lingodbhava.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.lingodbhava.textLayer }}" data-deity="Shiva" data-format="full" data-scripture="Shiva Purana" data-theme="Dharma" id="story-infinite-shiva-linga"><figure><img alt="A black stone Shiva linga before an infinite golden column, with a white hamsa feather, boar hoofprints, rudraksha and a pale ketaki flower" height="900" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/infinite-shiva-linga-card.webp" width="1600"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SHIVA / THE IMMEASURABLE</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.lingodbhava.textLayer }}</p><h3>The Appearance of the Infinite Shiva Linga</h3><p>Brahma and Vishnu seek the limits of a column of light whose beginning and end cannot be found.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.lingodbhava.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.lingodbhava.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#infinite-shiva-linga">Shiva Purana, Vidyeshvara Samhita 5–9</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.andhaka.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.andhaka.textLayer }}" data-deity="Shiva" data-format="full" data-scripture="Shiva Purana" data-theme="Transformation" id="story-shiva-andhakasura"><figure><img src="/assets/images/andhakasura-card.webp" alt="A crown and mace laid beside rudraksha, a white lotus and lamp as a trident shadow reaches toward dawn" width="1254" height="1254" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SHIVA &amp; ANDHAKA / TRANSFORMATION</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.andhaka.textLayer }}</p><h3>Shiva and Andhakasura</h3><p>Power mistakes desire for a right until conflict, consequence and recognition open another path among Shiva’s Ganas.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.andhaka.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.andhaka.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#shiva-andhakasura">Shiva Purana, Yuddha Khanda 42, 44–49</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.rama.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.rama.textLayer }}" data-deity="Rama" data-format="full" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Dharma" id="story-rama-exile"><figure><img alt="Rama, Sita and Lakshmana leaving Ayodhya for the forest" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/rama-exile.webp"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">RAMA / DHARMA</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.rama.textLayer }}</p><h3>Rama leaves Ayodhya</h3><p>A royal coronation gives way to exile, and a family must face the meaning of duty.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.rama.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.rama.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-rama-exile">Ramayana, Ayodhya Kanda</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.jatayu.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.jatayu.textLayer }}" data-deity="Rama" data-format="full" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Courage" id="story-jatayu-sacrifice"><figure><img src="/assets/images/jatayu-sacrifice-card.webp" alt="A great vulture feather beside a broken golden chariot wheel and bow in a forest at dawn" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">JATAYU / COURAGE</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.jatayu.textLayer }}</p><h3>Jatayu’s Sacrifice</h3><p>An aged guardian confronts Ravana, protects Sita and preserves the truth that will guide Rama’s search.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.jatayu.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.jatayu.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#jatayu-sacrifice">Valmiki Ramayana, Aranya Kanda 14, 50–51 and 68–69</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.hanuman.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.hanuman.textLayer }}" data-deity="Hanuman" data-format="full" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Courage" id="story-hanuman-lanka"><figure><img alt="Hanuman crossing the ocean toward Lanka in search of Sita" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/hanuman-lanka.webp" width="1536"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">HANUMAN / COURAGE</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.hanuman.textLayer }}</p><h3>Hanuman’s leap to Lanka</h3><p>Across the ocean lies the next step in the search for Sita.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.hanuman.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.hanuman.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-hanuman-lanka">Ramayana, Sundara Kanda</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.govardhana.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.govardhana.textLayer }}" data-deity="Krishna" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-govardhana"><figure><img alt="Krishna lifting Govardhana to shelter villagers and cattle from the rain" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/govardhana.webp"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">KRISHNA / PROTECTION</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.govardhana.textLayer }}</p><h3>Krishna lifts Govardhana</h3><p>A mountain becomes a shelter for the people and cattle of Vraja.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.govardhana.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.govardhana.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-govardhana">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 10, chapters 24–27</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.kaliya.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.kaliya.textLayer }}" data-deity="Krishna" data-format="full" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-kaliya"><figure><img src="/assets/images/krishna-kaliya-card.webp" alt="A peacock feather, flute and golden footprints beside clear Yamuna water with a peaceful cobra shadow below" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">KRISHNA / RESTORATION</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.kaliya.textLayer }}</p><h3>Krishna and Kaliya</h3><p>Krishna enters Kaliya’s poisoned lake, restores the Yamuna and joins decisive strength to mercy.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.kaliya.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.kaliya.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#krishna-kaliya">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 10, chapters 16–17</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.gajendra.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.gajendra.textLayer }}" data-deity="Vishnu" data-format="full" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Devotion" id="story-gajendra-moksha"><figure><img alt="An elephant trunk raising a lotus beside a conch and chakra at an imagined Trikuta lake" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/gajendra-moksha-card.webp" width="1536"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">VISHNU / SURRENDER</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.gajendra.textLayer }}</p><h3>Gajendra Moksha</h3><p>An elephant king’s strength fails in the water, an ancient prayer returns, and Vishnu answers.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.gajendra.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.gajendra.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#gajendra-moksha">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 8, chapters 2–4</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.matsya.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.matsya.textLayer }}" data-deity="Vishnu" data-format="full" data-scripture="Matsya Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-matsya-flood"><figure><img src="/assets/images/matsya-flood-card.webp" alt="A one-horned fish emblem, seed vessel, wrapped palm-leaf manuscripts and serpent-shaped ceremonial rope beside calm flood waters" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">MATSYA / PRESERVATION</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.matsya.textLayer }}</p><h3>Matsya Avatara · The Great Cosmic Flood</h3><p>Vishnu appears as a divine fish and guides Manu, living forms and sacred knowledge through the cosmic deluge.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.matsya.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.matsya.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#matsya-flood">Matsya Purana, Adi Khanda 1–2</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.varaha.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.varaha.textLayer }}" data-deity="Vishnu" data-format="full" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-varaha-earth"><figure><img alt="Four-armed Varaha in cosmic waters holding the discus, conch, mace and lotus while lifting the Earth" height="1206" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/varaha-rescue-card.webp" width="1600"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">VISHNU / RESTORATION</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.varaha.textLayer }}</p><h3>Varaha · The Rescue of the Earth</h3><p>Vishnu manifests as the divine boar, raises the Earth from the cosmic waters and confronts Hiranyaksha.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.varaha.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.varaha.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#varaha-earth">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 3, chapters 13 and 17–19</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.prahlada.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.prahlada.textLayer }}" data-deity="Vishnu" data-format="full" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Devotion" id="story-prahlada-narasimha"><figure><img alt="A carved palace pillar split open at twilight with a golden lion-shaped radiance, lotus and tulsi mala" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/prahlada-narasimha-card.webp" width="1536"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">PRAHLADA &amp; NARASIMHA / DEVOTION</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.prahlada.textLayer }}</p><h3>Prahlada and Narasimha</h3><p>A ruler tries to command his son’s devotion, and a pillar reveals a form no condition could contain.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.prahlada.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.prahlada.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#prahlada-narasimha">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 7, chapters 3–10</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.vamana.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.vamana.textLayer }}" data-deity="Vishnu" data-format="full" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Dharma" id="story-vamana-king-bali"><figure><img alt="A brahmachari parasol, staff and water vessels beside three luminous footprints leading into a cosmic indigo opening" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/vamana-three-steps-card.webp" width="1536"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">VAMANA &amp; KING BALI / DHARMA</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.vamana.textLayer }}</p><h3>Vamana and King Bali</h3><p>A small brahmachari asks for three steps of land, and the promise expands to the scale of the cosmos.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.vamana.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.vamana.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#vamana-king-bali">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 8, chapters 15–23</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.mahamaya.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.mahamaya.textLayer }}" data-deity="Devi" data-format="full" data-scripture="Markandeya Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-mahamaya-madhu-kaitabha"><figure><img src="/assets/images/mahamaya-madhu-kaitabha-card.webp" alt="A luminous white lotus, golden discus and crossed maces above a coiled cosmic serpent on the dark ocean" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">MAHAMAYA / AWAKENING</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.mahamaya.textLayer }}</p><h3>Mahamaya, Madhu and Kaitabha</h3><p>The Goddess withdraws cosmic sleep from Vishnu and turns the asuras’ pride into the opening for their defeat.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.mahamaya.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.mahamaya.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#mahamaya-madhu-kaitabha">Markandeya Purana, Devi Mahatmya 1</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.mahishasura.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.mahishasura.textLayer }}" data-deity="Devi" data-format="full" data-scripture="Markandeya Purana" data-theme="Courage" id="story-mahishasura"><figure><img alt="Durga riding her lion before Mahishasura in buffalo form" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/durga-mahishasura.webp"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">DEVI / COURAGE</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.mahishasura.textLayer }}</p><h3>Devi and Mahishasura</h3><p>The gods’ combined radiance takes divine form in the struggle against Mahishasura.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.mahishasura.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.mahishasura.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-mahishasura">Markandeya Purana, Devi Mahatmya</a></p></div></article>
<article class="collection-card" data-collections="{{ storyCatalog.shumbha.collections | join(' ') }}" data-text-layer="{{ storyCatalog.shumbha.textLayer }}" data-deity="Devi" data-format="full" data-scripture="Markandeya Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-shumbha-nishumbha"><figure><img alt="A lion, ritual bell and red banner on an imagined Himalayan ridge beneath seven lights converging into one" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/shumbha-nishumbha-card.webp" width="1536"/></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">DEVI / PROTECTION</p><p class="story-text-layer">{{ storyCatalog.shumbha.textLayer }}</p><h3>Devi and Shumbha–Nishumbha</h3><p>Many divine powers arise for one struggle, then return into the Goddess before the final conflict.</p><p class="story-card-meta"><span>Full story</span><span>{{ storyCatalog.shumbha.minutes }} min read</span></p><a class="tale-card-link" href="{{ storyCatalog.shumbha.href }}">Read the story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#devi-shumbha-nishumbha">Markandeya Purana, Devi Mahatmya 5–11</a></p></div></article>
